invariant: INV-26
file: src/quic.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: ch_quic_initial_keys writes a byte of the TLS traffic secret into
  the round keys of a stored Initial key, which is the shape that
  defeated inv-26-aes-public-keys-only for as long as ch_quic held two
  aes_public_key values: the write is neither a call nor an initializer,
  so no Semgrep branch reads it, and quic_initial.c then hands that
  struct to aes_encrypt_block as a permitted caller. ch_quic now stores
  the Destination Connection ID and no key, so initial_tx does not exist
  and the compiler refuses the line. The refusal is the check.

